      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Draft and finalise the daily inspection checklist and weekly routine",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Alright everyone, here's the first draft of the 'Daily Vehicle Inspection Checklist' (A1) for the pilot. Let me know what you think. I tried to cover the main points without making it too long. This is for T1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Looks ok to me. Covers tyres, lights, brakes.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Should we add 'check engine oil'?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "It's under 'Fluid Levels'.",
            "mentions": [
              108987
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "This is a good start. From my time as a mover, we always had to check the lift gate hydraulics and the container securing straps daily. They can fail suddenly. We should add those.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "That's a great point, @38857. Those are critical safety items. However, checking hydraulics daily might be too time-consuming and slow down departures, which is a risk we need to manage. What if we keep the daily check for a quick visual on straps and leaks, but move the detailed hydraulic pressure check to the weekly deep-check routine we're defining in T2?",
            "mentions": [
              38857
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "That makes sense. Daily list stays fast, weekly list is more thorough. I like it. So, daily is just a visual check of straps and for any obvious hydraulic leaks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Ok, I can agree with that. As long as it's checked properly once a week.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Exactly. This also helps with T7, mapping current steps and removing redundant actions. We avoid a full hydraulic check every single day. So, are we all happy with the proposed structure for the daily checklist A1? It will cover: Exterior (lights, tyres, glass), Interior (horn, brakes, steering), Fluids (visual check), and Safety (straps visual, fire extinguisher).",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Approved. I'll update A1 with these sections and we can use this version for the pilot on Monday.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "yes good",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Excellent. So to summarize: the daily checklist A1 structure is approved (D3), and we've agreed that detailed checks like hydraulics will be part of the weekly routine from T2, not the daily one (D4). Great progress.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D3",
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D3",
            "D4"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
            {
              "task_id": "T1",
