      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Agree on hazardous substances handling rules and workshop standards",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Next up: the state of the workshop. The chemical cabinet is a mess and tools are left everywhere. We need to get this sorted as part of T3 and T9. We need some simple rules that everyone can follow.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "Yeah it's always messy. I can never find the right spanner.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "For the chemicals, we should have separate marked shelves for oils, degreasers, and brake fluids. When I handled cleaning agents before, we had a color code system. Red for corrosive, yellow for flammable. It was easy to see what was dangerous.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "That's a fantastic, practical idea. Let's formalize that. We'll create the 'Hazardous Substances Handling and Storage Guide' (A2). It will include your color-coding system, mandatory PPE for each chemical type, and simple spill response steps. This will satisfy T3 and get us sign-off from the H&S officer. Everyone on board with this approach?",
            "mentions": [
              38857
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Yes, color coding is smart. I can make the labels for the shelves.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "sounds good",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Great, that's settled then. Now for the tools and general cleanliness (T9). I propose we create a simple 'Workshop Cleaning and Tool Storage Standard' (A6). It will have two parts: 1. A shadow board for all common tools so we know where they go. 2. A 10-minute tidy-up at the end of every shift, including sweeping your bay and wiping down surfaces. Thoughts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "A shadow board would be great. So we know what's missing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "End of shift clean up is a good habit. Keeps the place safe.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "I can build the shadow board next week if we get the materials.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Perfect. So we have two decisions. D5: We'll adopt the color-coded system for chemicals and document it in A2. D6: We'll implement a shadow board for tools and a mandatory end-of-shift tidy-up, documented in A6. I'll draft the text for both guides.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5",
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D5",
            "D6"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
