      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Define how incidents, near-misses and \"do not use\" vehicles are flagged",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Someone left an oil patch near bay 2, almost slipped. Where do I write this down?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Good question. We need that new log from T5. I can make a quick sheet for now.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Hold on, let's do this right from the start to avoid confusion. This is exactly what T5 is for. Let's define the official 'Incident and Near-Miss Reporting Log' (A4) right now. I propose it must have these fields: Date, Time, Location, Vehicle ID (if any), Description of Incident, and Immediate Action Taken. We'll keep a printed binder by the supervisor's desk. Agreed?",
            "mentions": [
              109283
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Ok, that's better. A standard format is good. I'll create the template in Excel with those fields.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 156061,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "yes that works",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "This is good for logs, but what about when a truck is unsafe to drive? Like with a major brake issue. We just leave a note on the dash now, but sometimes it gets lost or the next shift misses it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Excellent point. That's a huge risk and exactly what T11 is meant to solve. A paper note is not reliable enough. How about we use large, red, magnetic 'DO NOT USE' tags? We can stick them right on the driver's side door handle. They're highly visible, reusable, and won't get lost.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 108987,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Tags are a good idea. No one can miss a big red tag.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 109283,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Love it. Simple and effective. I can order a pack of 10.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 38857,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Yes, that would work much better.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 203126,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Okay, decisions made. D7: The incident log A4 will use the fields I listed and be kept at the supervisor's desk. D8: We will use red magnetic 'DO NOT USE' tags on the driver's door to mark unsafe vehicles. Great work, team.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7",
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
          "decisions_made": [
            "D7",
            "D8"
          ],
          "next_steps": [
